`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:[e.jsx(i.strong,{children:"Revocation."})," In initial enrollment the client certificate and every intermediate CA between it and the validation CA are checked, each against its issuer; extra certificates the device sends in the handshake are ignored. Certificates managed by Lamassu are checked against their stored status, and external ones through their OCSP and CRL endpoints. The operation fails closed when revocation cannot be verified: unreachable endpoints, stale or invalid evidence and inconclusive statuses always reject the certificate. A validation CA that is revoked in Lamassu also rejects the operation, without falling back to the remaining validation CAs. ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/est/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks",children:"Revocation and checks"})," details the evidence the endpoints must present.",e.jsx(i.ins,{className:"lm-diff-ins",children:" CRL lists fetched for these checks are reused for a limited time before being downloaded again; see "}),e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/est/bootstrap-identity#revocation-and-checks",children:e.jsx(i.ins,{className:"lm-diff-ins",children:"Revocation and checks"})}),e.jsx(i.ins,{className:"lm-diff-ins",children:" for the caching window and its effect on revocation visibility."})]}),`
